From 5ecbb476e206b676c7bb89bc7f0e81a5ef0a73fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:57:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] wait-check --gateway: a fresh Board replica may turn
 an unreachable-owner answer into met

Post-merge check t_01a1d5c30d953d84 of #2370 found 0 of 2 expedited cross-gateway parks woke on the
change (t_01a1d5ead059278d). Both parks probed `hermes kanban wait-check task X --gateway G`. From pool
workers ssh to G fails (name not resolved / Permission denied, rc 255), so check_remote fell back to the
hermes-hub registry replica only (collector-refreshed). The expedite is triggered by this gateway's Board
sync replica (sync-shadow), which runs minutes ahead: the expedited probe read the old `running`, went
back to cadence, and both parks slept the full 900 s check_every (condition_met 914 s / 915 s after the
expedite). The #2370 test parked on `wait-check task X` without `--gateway`, so it never hit this path.

Fix (option 1 of the card): when the owner gateway cannot be asked (OSError/timeout, rc 255, or the
forced-command refusal) a task check reads the registry replica exactly as before, and when that answer
is not met (rc 1, 2 or 3) and was not a live owner read, it also reads this gateway's Board replica row
(the same Board row G's own wait-check falls back to). Only a Board answer of met (rc 0) is taken, and only
when that replica was pulled to the feed head within kanban_replica_freshness.FRESH_SECONDS (600 s) with no
future stamp, judged by the same verdict as check_local (--from/--until/parked-agent).

The Board replica only moves the answer toward met (review t_01a1d603304c96f3 of the first head
001fdb313b, which weighed observed_at against pulled_at and regressed two cases):
- it never downgrades the registry's met: pulled_at is this gateway's pull time, not when the owner wrote
  the row, so a row pulled seconds ago can still lag the owner's push;
- it never replaces the registry's rc 3 (stale or unknown scope) with not-yet: an offline owner's Board row
  is frozen however recently we pulled it, and rc 3 is what wakes the park as gateway_offline at
  STALE_WAKE_AFTER.
No cross-host clock comparison remains, so kanban_wait_replica is unchanged. A Board met over a newer
registry not-yet is what the no-`--gateway` probe of that same row already reports.

Why not option 2 (re-arm the expedite once more): it only shortens the lag to the registry's next
collector refresh (minutes) and adds a probe per change; reading the copy that triggered the expedite
answers on the first probe. No new polling: the extra read happens only inside a probe that already ran
and did not answer met.

Tests:
- test_kanban_awaited_card_wake.py::test_gateway_probe_wakes_on_the_board_change_while_ssh_fails_and_the_registry_lags
  (the live shape: `--gateway`, ssh rc 255, registry fresh but lagging) RED on main (park still
  scheduled), GREEN here; plus a not-fresh Board replica keeps the registry's not-yet and the cadence.
- test_kanban_wait_check_board_replica.py: fresh Board met wins over a lagging registry (any scope age),
  never downgrades a registry met, stale registry + fresh Board not-yet stays rc 3, stale/future/unreadable
  Board replica adds nothing, --from on the Board view, live owner read stands. The 3 regression tests for
  the review's findings are RED on 001fdb313b, GREEN here.
- All 25 test files referencing wait-check / kanban_wait_check / kanban_wait_replica: 848 passed, 1 skipped.
